{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793662406129324001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"healthful-childlike-aruanas","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"88bb070fc38a1c207e4eba3272c0a4bc6a4338922c1a6a2c5cffc1f00cf82a03","event_uuid":"0777e45a-a87b-4503-bcc7-88e5f91e6457","position":{"commit_sha":"1d864a1a4f7006973cb3a867b3e255303c74d85b","position":"1793647951591128729-0777e45a-a87b-4503-bcc7-88e5f91e6457"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"dd0b3e9fd7bec65026437a8a163636c5cf54d6243ada23d3473fe44a89c9d718","event_uuid":"f8723e49-f23d-42c8-8c5a-b871a1fc7fe6","position":{"commit_sha":"50a068e0e5d109d9ef2db1dac92b152e6a41c3f7","position":"1793648073423277817-f8723e49-f23d-42c8-8c5a-b871a1fc7fe6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"a06a276b7b3970ac293301cc623df78f14e346a747afe6a449f1f9acad412aaa","event_uuid":"a3b2795a-8776-4524-9035-77cf1d1a3644","position":{"commit_sha":"e6520225fde197342b6461c1ec681fc63440aac1","position":"1793649760230912484-a3b2795a-8776-4524-9035-77cf1d1a3644"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"dd28c9561cb3b5e54f97bf93237544563b8d2977ad1493691c2c36775936f073","event_uuid":"d0b70567-8279-48b6-8987-a7af831a4436","position":{"commit_sha":"b4f9730bb79d1790b99e9526ec201b4cbab2b15e","position":"1793649871439076217-d0b70567-8279-48b6-8987-a7af831a4436"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793647951591128729,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f8723e49-f23d-42c8-8c5a-b871a1fc7fe6","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"fe94-2e22-ea9e-46f7"}],"description":"## Parent\n\nEpic `77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec`, authorized at full scope by the operator on 2026-11-02.\nThis is deliverable 2. Depends on `fe94-2e22-ea9e-46f7`, which establishes the\nnet-mechanism criterion this story's own change must satisfy.\n\n## The gap\n\nA mechanism admitted by a `# mechanism-ok:` marker is admitted FOREVER. Measured at\n`origin/main` `4cf1ae42946`:\n\n- The marker grammar is `scripts/_mechanism_delta/markers.py:20` (`_MARKER_RE`), separators\n  at `markers.py:23` — `(\"—\", \"--\", \"-\", \":\")` — and the capture at `markers.py:42-43`. It\n  has exactly three fields: kind, name, reason. The reason is free text.\n- `scripts/_mechanism_delta/compare.py:89-92` admits a `new` key when the marker's reason is\n  nonblank. `compare.py:83` makes a blank reason an error.\n- Nothing parses a ticket id out of the reason. Nothing checks that a referenced ticket\n  exists, is open, or ever closes.\n\nSo an agent writes `# mechanism-ok: env_var REBAR_X — temporary, remove after the migration`\nand the mechanism is permanently blessed. The migration closes; the marker stays; the\nratchet never looks again. The admission is a one-way door with no expiry.\n\n## The convention already exists — it is simply not parsed or enforced\n\nMeasured across the real admission sites (`src/`, `infra/`, `.github/`, the four\n`scripts/` checkers, the four `tests/_*` helpers and the `Makefile`), excluding the\ngrammar's own definition in `markers.py`, `compare.py`, `check_mechanism_delta.py`,\n`tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py`, `docs/architecture.md` and `AGENTS.md`:\n\n- **87 real-site markers.**\n- **72 of them already name a ticket id** in the reason text, e.g.\n  `# mechanism-ok: ci_gate .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml::Wait before retrying\n  Gerrit patchset checkout — 1e24-bfc0 in-job retry keeps transient Gerrit transport\n  faults from causing false Verified -1 votes.`\n- **15 do not name a two-quad or four-quad id.** Of those, most name a **deprecated\n  4-digit single-quad** (`c6ce`, `aa9e`, `adab`, `5169`) or a Jira id (`REB-640`); one is\n  the `Makefile` line that documents the grammar rather than admitting anything.\n\nThis sharpens the defect. AGENTS.md records that a bare 4-digit quad is deprecated as a\nreference form because \"in a store of any size those quads collide, so they resolve to\nnothing.\" Those markers therefore cite a ticket that cannot be resolved — a sunset\nreference that already fails to mean anything, with nothing to detect it.\n\nThe ratchet baseline carries **647 mechanisms** (`.github/mechanism-baseline.json`,\n`mechanisms` key), so 87 marker-admitted mechanisms sit against roughly 560 grandfathered\nentries. This story governs the admitted set, not the grandfathered one.\n\n## The change\n\nTwo halves.\n\n**Half 1 — the marker names a sunset ticket.** Narrow the admission grammar so the third\nfield opens with a resolvable rebar ticket id rather than arbitrary prose. A marker whose\nid does not resolve is not an admission, and the ratchet fails as it would for a blank\nreason. A bare 4-digit quad does not resolve and so is not accepted.\n\n**Half 2 — that ticket cannot close while the marker remains.** Add a deterministic\nprecheck to the completion-verification close path: when the ticket being closed is named\nas the sunset ticket of a `# mechanism-ok:` marker still present in the tree, the close is\nrefused and the refusal names the marker's file and line.\n\n## What this retires\n\nRequired by `fe94`'s net-mechanism criterion, which this story is the first change to be\njudged by.\n\nThis change ADDS one deterministic close precheck. It RETIRES the free-text reason as an\naccepted admission: after this change the only thing that admits a new mechanism is a\nresolvable ticket id, so the \"write any sentence and pass\" path at `compare.py:89-92`\nceases to exist. The admission surface narrows rather than grows — one admission form\nreplaces one admission form, plus the enforcement that makes the new form mean something.\n\n## Where the close refusal goes\n\nThe close gate has NO pluggable deterministic check — measured, not assumed. There is no\n`_PRECHECKS` tuple and no registry of precheck callables in\n`src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py`. Unlike plan review, which has\n`det_invariants.run_project_det_checks` driven by `exec: \"DET\"` overlay entries, the close\npath has no project-pluggable equivalent.\n\nThe seam is the straight-line call sequence inside `_completion_precheck`, which runs its\nrefusal points in order BEFORE the LLM verifier is invoked at `close_precheck.py:694`. The\nexisting landing check is `close_precheck.py:151` `_check_work_landed`, called at\n`close_precheck.py:685`, raising at `close_precheck.py:215-222`. A new refusal is one more\ncall in that sequence and needs no restructuring.\n\nPrecedent that a precheck may read repository state beyond git history:\n`close_precheck.py:289` `_check_file_impact_vs_diff` reads landed commits' diffs. The\nsunset scan reads tracked file contents, which is a wider read than any existing precheck\nperforms, so the plan states that explicitly rather than letting review infer it.\n\n## The --force caveat, stated rather than hidden\n\n`close_precheck.py:634-637` short-circuits the ENTIRE precheck block via\n`_gate_skip_expectation` when `--force=\"<reason>\"` is passed. No deterministic close\nrefusal in this gate is unconditional, and this one will not be either. The acceptance\ncriteria below are therefore worded as refusal absent a human override, not as an absolute\nbar. Per AGENTS.md agents must not use `--force`; the override is a human operator's\njudgement call and is audited by the absence of a signed attestation.\n\n## Portability\n\nPer the blocking `project.portability` criterion, a check whose only trigger is a specific\nCI system is not portable. Half 2 runs in-process in the close path with no CI dependency,\nso it fires in any environment that can close a ticket. Half 1 runs inside\n`scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py`, which `make lint` invokes locally and which CI also\ninvokes; its trigger is the lint target, not a CI provider, so it fires with no CI present.\n\n## Provider neutrality\n\nBoth halves are deterministic. Neither calls an LLM, so there is no provider or model\ndependency to be neutral about. This is stated so review does not assume an LLM path.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A `# mechanism-ok:` marker whose reason does not open with a resolvable ticket id\n      does not admit its mechanism: `scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits\n      non-zero for a new mechanism carrying such a marker. Verified by a test.\n- [ ] A bare 4-digit single-quad is not accepted as a resolvable id. Verified by a test.\n- [ ] A marker whose reason opens with a resolvable ticket id admits its mechanism and\n      `--check` exits zero. Verified by a test.\n- [ ] Closing a ticket named as the sunset ticket of a marker still present in the tree is\n      refused absent a human `--force` override, and the error names the marker's file and\n      line. Verified by a test.\n- [ ] Closing that same ticket succeeds once the marker is removed from the tree. Verified\n      by a test.\n- [ ] Closing a ticket named by NO marker is unaffected — the new precheck does not fire.\n      Verified by a test.\n- [ ] Removing a mechanism still passes the ratchet. Verified by a test, guarding the\n      shrink-only asymmetry at `compare.py:99` where `counters.stale` is never consulted.\n- [ ] All 15 real-site markers that do not currently name a resolvable id are migrated to\n      one, and the remaining 72 are confirmed to parse under the narrowed grammar.\n      Verified by `make verify`.\n- [ ] The new precheck fires with no CI provider present. Verified by a test that\n      exercises it with no CI environment configured.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes.\n\n## Measurement base\n\nEvery citation and count above was read from `origin/main` at `4cf1ae42946`. Line numbers\nare from that commit. The 87/72/15 split was measured by scanning the real admission sites\ndirectly, not sampled.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","fe94-2e22-ea9e-46f7"],["parent","77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"77e3-28e2-31ec-47ec","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["complexity-reduction"],"ticket_id":"d68f-4771-ebc1-4ee4","ticket_type":"story","title":"Enforce mechanism sunset: markers name a sunset ticket, and that ticket cannot close while the marker remains","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0777e45a-a87b-4503-bcc7-88e5f91e6457","f8723e49-f23d-42c8-8c5a-b871a1fc7fe6","a3b2795a-8776-4524-9035-77cf1d1a3644","d0b70567-8279-48b6-8987-a7af831a4436"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793662406129324001,"uuid":"33d14326-cb46-49d5-86a5-9d65fcd79b2d"}